  "answer": "The limitations of Mendeleev’s periodic table include the presence of anomalous pairs of elements, where elements with higher atomic weights were placed before those with lower atomic weights, and dissimilar elements were placed together in the same group. The modern periodic table addresses these limitations by arranging elements based on their atomic numbers instead of atomic weights, which eliminates the problem of anomalous series and ensures that elements with similar properties are grouped together.",
